speechtext:
Yes. This is an excerpt
from the report of the chief post office superintendent made in 1920:	Population 1,640;
four industrial concerns employing about 300 hands; two banks; sixteen stores. The post office is located in a building, one of a block of stores. The floor space is 650 square feet, of which the public lobby comprises 350 square feet,' leaving a working space of only 300 square feet. The carriers working in the office are not separated from the rest of the staff. It is recommended that more space be provided.
